{
 "bio": {
  "lang": "en",
  "script": "Latn",
  "text": "Dr. Alemayehu Wassie Eshete is an Ethiopian forest ecologist, conservation scientist, and author internationally recognized for his pioneering research on Ethiopian Orthodox Church forests. With over 30 years of experience, he has contributed extensively to forest ecology, biodiversity conservation, and environmental restoration. He is the author of Ethiopian Orthodox Church Forests: Opportunities and Challenges for Restoration (2007) and the Amharic novel Emegua, Ziguara & Merbebit. His work bridges science, culture, and faith-based environmental stewardship, positioning him as a leading voice in sustainable restoration and conservation in Ethiopia."
 },
